      <div class="invisible-main-faq-page-container">
        <div class="main-faq-page-container">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Question</h2>
          <div
            id="wholequestion1"
            class="whole-question-main-box"
            style="margin-top: 30px"
          >
            <div class="whole-questio-main-box-separation-line"></div>
            <div class="container-question-and-icon">
              <div class="main-faq-page-container-question">
                What does your website do?
              </div>
              <div class="main-faq-page-icon-container">
                <i
                  id="arbtn1"
                  style="cursor: pointer"
                  class="ri-arrow-down-s-line"
                ></i>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div id="ans1" class="answer-main-container">
              We use machine learning to predict if a scheduled appointment will
              result in a "no-show," helping businesses proactively manage their
              schedules and resources.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="wholequestion2" class="whole-question-main-box">
            <div class="whole-questio-main-box-separation-line"></div>
            <div class="container-question-and-icon">
              <div class="main-faq-page-container-question">
                How does your prediction model work?
              </div>
              <div class="main-faq-page-icon-container">
                <i
                  id="arbtn2"
                  style="cursor: pointer"
                  class="ri-arrow-down-s-line"
                ></i>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              id="ans2"
              style="display: none"
              id="ans1"
              class="answer-main-container"
            >
              Our model analyzes your historical appointment data, identifying
              patterns and factors that indicate a higher likelihood of a
              no-show for future appointments.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="wholequestion3" class="whole-question-main-box">
            <div class="whole-questio-main-box-separation-line"></div>
            <div class="container-question-and-icon">
              <div class="main-faq-page-container-question">
                How accurate are the predictions?
              </div>
              <div class="main-faq-page-icon-container">
                <i
                  id="arbtn3"
                  style="cursor: pointer"
                  class="ri-arrow-down-s-line"
                ></i>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              id="ans3"
              style="display: none"
              id="ans1"
              class="answer-main-container"
            >
              Our model accurately predicts no-shows with 79% accuracy. It also
              boasts 82% precision and 80% f1-score, ensuring reliable insights
              for your scheduling needs.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="wholequestion4" class="whole-question-main-box">
            <div class="whole-questio-main-box-separation-line"></div>
            <div class="container-question-and-icon">
              <div class="main-faq-page-container-question">
                How can I fine tune this model?
              </div>
              <div class="main-faq-page-icon-container">
                <i
                  id="arbtn4"
                  style="cursor: pointer"
                  class="ri-arrow-down-s-line"
                ></i>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              id="ans4"
              style="display: none"
              id="ans1"
              class="answer-main-container"
            >
              This model is for project demonstration only and cannot be
              fine-tuned directly. However, you can train your own model using
              our processed dataset to achieve similar predictions.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="wholequestion5" class="whole-question-main-box">
            <div class="whole-questio-main-box-separation-line"></div>
            <div class="container-question-and-icon">
              <div class="main-faq-page-container-question">
                What kind of data do I need to provide?
              </div>
              <div class="main-faq-page-icon-container">
                <i
                  id="arbtn5"
                  style="cursor: pointer"
                  class="ri-arrow-down-s-line"
                ></i>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              id="ans5"
              style="display: none"
              id="ans1"
              class="answer-main-container"
            >
              Typically, we utilize anonymous historical appointment data,
              including dates, times, patient/client demographics
              (non-identifying), appointment types, and previous show/no-show
              statuses.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="wholequestion6" class="whole-question-main-box">
            <div class="whole-questio-main-box-separation-line"></div>
            <div class="container-question-and-icon">
              <div class="main-faq-page-container-question">
                Who can benefit from this model?
              </div>
              <div class="main-faq-page-icon-container">
                <i
                  id="arbtn6"
                  style="cursor: pointer"
                  class="ri-arrow-down-s-line"
                ></i>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              id="ans6"
              style="display: none"
              id="ans1"
              class="answer-main-container"
            >
              Any business reliant on scheduled appointments, including
              healthcare clinics, salons, dental offices, and even service
              providers, can significantly benefit from our insights.
            </div>
          </div>
